            <ArticleTitle>Tubular Carcinoma of the Breast: Advantages and Limitations of Breast Tomosynthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3906195</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2016/3906195</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tubular carcinoma of the breast is a rare variant of invasive ductal carcinoma. We report a case of 42-year-old asymptomatic female with a histopathological proven multifocal tubular carcinoma, studied by mammography, Tomosynthesis, Ultrasound, and Magnetic Resonance. Herein, we discuss the advantages and limitations of Tomosynthesis, an emerging imaging technique, in this particular case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
